<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "System Data" field-work statistics readout (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual PARITY reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Field/FormFieldData`
    (source: FormFieldData.cs + FormFieldData.Designer.cs + FormFieldData.resx), per AAP §0.3.3 —
    never a redesign. It is a narrow, modeless panel shown alongside the running app that displays
    live field-work statistics (worked / applied area, remaining area + time, overlap %, work rate
    and trip area / distance), refreshed once per second.

    CODE-BEHIND CONTRACT — FormFieldDataView.axaml.cs (partial class AgOpenGPS.Views.FormFieldDataView : Window):
      * IMPERATIVE, not MVVM — intentionally NO x:DataType, no DataContext, no {Binding}. The original
        WinForms timer1_Tick (System.Windows.Forms.Timer, Interval = 1000 ms) updated each value Label
        by name; the code-behind reproduces that with an Avalonia DispatcherTimer that addresses the
        x:Name'd value TextBlocks below directly, reading the pre-formatted strings from the injected
        CFieldData (mf.fd). The original ctor was FormFieldData(Form callingForm); the code-behind keeps
        that reference-to-FormGPS pattern. The timer is non-visual, so it has no element in this markup.
      * The value x:Name's below ARE that contract and MUST stay spelled exactly as the generated
        x:Name fields the code-behind references:
            lblWorkRate, lblApplied, lblActualLessOverlap, lblOverlapPercent,
            labelAreaValue, labelDistanceDriven,
          and the boundary-gated "Remain" group values:
            lblTotalArea, lblAreaRemain, lblTimeRemaining, lblRemainPercent, lblActualRemain.
      * Caption text is (re)assigned at runtime from gStr in the original ctor
        (labelTotal=gsTotal+":", labelWorked=gsWorked, labelApplied/labelApplied2=gsApplied+":",
         labelRemain/labelRemain2=gsRemain+":", labelOverlap=gsOverlap+":", labelActual=gsActual,
         labelRate=gsRate+":", labelArea=gsArea+":", labelDistance=gsDistance+":"). The English text
        below is the verbatim Designer placeholder the code-behind overrides — kept (not blanked) so the
        design-time preview and the no-translation fallback are correct, mirroring the accepted sibling
        FormSaveOrNotView. labelTrip ("Trip") and the three divider rules (label1 / label7 / label2)
        are NOT touched by the ctor, so their appearance is fixed here.
      * Visibility: the "Remain" group — lblTotalArea, lblAreaRemain, lblTimeRemaining, lblRemainPercent,
        lblActualRemain plus the captions labelRemain / labelRemain2 — is shown only when a field
        boundary exists (mf.bnd.bndList.Count > 0). FormFieldData_Load calls timer1_Tick immediately, so
        the code-behind sets these IsVisible states authoritatively on first paint; they default visible
        here (Designer parity) and the code-behind collapses them when no boundary is present.
      * btnTripReset_Click resets the trip totals (mf.fd.workedAreaTotalUser = 0; mf.fd.distanceUser = 0).

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormFieldData.Designer.cs:
      Text "System Data"            -> Title
      ClientSize 197 x 483          -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window)
      FormBorderStyle.None          -> SystemDecorations="None"
      MaximizeBox/MinimizeBox false -> CanResize="False"
      ShowInTaskbar = false         -> ShowInTaskbar="False"
      (StartPosition default)       -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (owned panel over FormGPS)
      Font Tahoma 11.25 (default)   -> FontFamily="Tahoma", FontSize="15" (form default; per-row sizes below)

    THEME — the original drew Color.White text on a Color.Black BackColor. Per the assigned spec this
    view tracks the app day/night palette instead of hard-coding black/white: Background = AogFrameBrush
    and text = AogTextBrush, pulled from App.axaml's ThemeDictionaries via {DynamicResource} so the
    Light<->Dark switch is observed live. No WinForms / System.Drawing colours are referenced.

    Font sizes (WinForms points × 96/72 = Avalonia device-independent pixels):
      Tahoma 14.25 -> 19   (captions, value labels, section headers — the dominant size)
      Tahoma 12.75 -> 17   (labelAreaValue, labelDistanceDriven)
      Tahoma 11.25 -> 15   (form default)

    LAYOUT — the WinForms Designer used absolute Label positions; reproduced here as a single
    two-column Grid (Auto caption | * value) whose 18 row heights follow the Designer's top-to-bottom
    Y-deltas so every caption:value data row lands on its original Y. Within each "section header +
    divider" pair the combined Designer height is split to give the header room and let the rule sit
    cleanly beneath it (each pair's total is preserved, so the data rows below never move). The section
    headers ("Worked" / "Actual" / "Trip") and the divider rules span both columns; the boundary-gated
    "Remain" group occupies the rows between the Worked and Actual headers. The
    "____________________" separator labels (label1 / label7 / label2) are reproduced as thin themed
    Border rules rather than underscore glyphs.

    No WinForms, no System.Drawing, no OpenTK namespaces are referenced — Avalonia 11.3 markup only.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormFieldDataView"
        Title="System Data"
        Width="197"
        Height="483"
        CanResize="False"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        Padding="0"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}"
        Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="15">

    <Window.Styles>
        <!-- Base label rule: themed text colour, single-line, vertically centred. The dominant WinForms
             label size was Tahoma 14.25 (-> 19), so that is the base; the two trip values override to 17. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="NoWrap" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="19" />
        </Style>

        <!-- WinForms caption labels: FontStyle.Regular, left-aligned at the form's left margin. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.caption">
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Normal" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Left" />
        </Style>

        <!-- WinForms value labels: FontStyle.Bold, sat in the value column. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.value">
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Left" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Section headers ("Worked" / "Actual" / "Trip"): FontStyle.Regular, centred across both
             columns and vertically centred in their row so the divider rule in the next row sits
             cleanly beneath the caption (mirrors the WinForms header-with-underline grouping). -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.header">
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Normal" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Divider rules reproduce the WinForms "____________________" separator labels
             (label1 / label7 / label2) as thin, theme-aware horizontal lines. -->
        <Style Selector="Border.divider">
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="2" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Top" />
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,4,0" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Flat, chrome-less image button: reproduces the WinForms Button with a transparent BackColor
             and a single BackgroundImage (Resources.back_button). The :pointerover / :pressed template
             overrides suppress the Fluent hover / press surface so only the glyph shows. -->
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Single two-column Grid. Column 0 = caption (Auto, MinWidth 88 so the value column stays aligned
        regardless of caption length / translation); Column 1 = the live value. Row heights follow the
        Designer's top-to-bottom Y-deltas so every caption:value data row lands on its original Y; within
        each "section header + divider" pair the combined Designer height is split to give the header
        room and let the rule sit cleanly beneath it (the pair's total is preserved, so the data rows do
        not move). The final * row holds the centred reset button (WinForms 76 x 44).
    -->
    <Grid Margin="8,0,4,0"
          RowDefinitions="29,24,13,29,28,30,36,24,16,29,29,38,32,19,6,25,29,*">
        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" MinWidth="88" />
            <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

        <!-- Row 0 — Total: | total field area. WinForms labelTotal @ (13,0) + lblTotalArea @ (99,0).
             lblTotalArea is part of the boundary-gated "Remain" group (hidden when no boundary). -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelTotal" Classes="caption" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Text="Total:" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblTotalArea" Classes="value" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 1 — "Worked" section header. WinForms labelWorked @ (71,29); text set to gStr.gsWorked. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelWorked" Classes="header" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Text="Worked" />

        <!-- Row 2 — divider (WinForms label1 @ (4,38) "____________________"). -->
        <Border x:Name="label1" Classes="divider" Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" />

        <!-- Row 3 — Applied: | worked applied area. WinForms labelApplied @ (13,66) + lblApplied @ (114,66). -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelApplied" Classes="caption" Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="0" Text="Applied:" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblApplied" Classes="value" Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 4 — Remain: | worked area remaining. WinForms labelRemain @ (12,95) + lblAreaRemain @ (114,95).
             Both are in the boundary-gated "Remain" group. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelRemain" Classes="caption" Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="0" Text="Remain:" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblAreaRemain" Classes="value" Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="1" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 5 — remaining percentage (no caption). WinForms lblRemainPercent @ (114,123). "Remain" group. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblRemainPercent" Classes="value" Grid.Row="5" Grid.Column="1" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 6 — estimated time remaining (no caption). WinForms lblTimeRemaining @ (114,153). "Remain" group. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblTimeRemaining" Classes="value" Grid.Row="6" Grid.Column="1" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 7 — "Actual" section header. WinForms labelActual @ (71,189); text set to gStr.gsActual. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelActual" Classes="header" Grid.Row="7" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Text="Actual" />

        <!-- Row 8 — divider (WinForms label7 @ (4,203) "____________________"). -->
        <Border x:Name="label7" Classes="divider" Grid.Row="8" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" />

        <!-- Row 9 — Applied: | actual area worked (less overlap). WinForms labelApplied2 @ (9,229) +
             lblActualLessOverlap @ (112,229). -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelApplied2" Classes="caption" Grid.Row="9" Grid.Column="0" Text="Applied:" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblActualLessOverlap" Classes="value" Grid.Row="9" Grid.Column="1" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 10 — Remain: | actual remaining. WinForms labelRemain2 @ (10,258) + lblActualRemain @ (113,258).
             Both are in the boundary-gated "Remain" group. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelRemain2" Classes="caption" Grid.Row="10" Grid.Column="0" Text="Remain:" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblActualRemain" Classes="value" Grid.Row="10" Grid.Column="1" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 11 — Overlap: | overlap percentage. WinForms labelOverlap @ (9,287) + lblOverlapPercent @ (113,287). -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelOverlap" Classes="caption" Grid.Row="11" Grid.Column="0" Text="Overlap:" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblOverlapPercent" Classes="value" Grid.Row="11" Grid.Column="1" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 12 — Rate: | work rate. WinForms labelRate @ (10,325) + lblWorkRate @ (101,325). -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelRate" Classes="caption" Grid.Row="12" Grid.Column="0" Text="Rate:" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblWorkRate" Classes="value" Grid.Row="12" Grid.Column="1" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 13 — "Trip" section header / caption for the reset button. WinForms labelTrip @ (59,357);
             NOT set by the ctor, so the literal "Trip" is kept here. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelTrip" Classes="header" Grid.Row="13" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Text="Trip" />

        <!-- Row 14 — divider (WinForms label2 @ (7,364) "____________________"). -->
        <Border x:Name="label2" Classes="divider" Grid.Row="14" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" />

        <!-- Row 15 — Area: | trip area (user). WinForms labelArea @ (10,382) + labelAreaValue @ (102,382),
             value font Tahoma 12.75 -> 17. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelArea" Classes="caption" Grid.Row="15" Grid.Column="0" Text="Area:" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelAreaValue" Classes="value" Grid.Row="15" Grid.Column="1" FontSize="17" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 16 — Dist: | trip distance driven. WinForms labelDistance @ (10,407) + labelDistanceDriven @ (102,407),
             value font Tahoma 12.75 -> 17. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelDistance" Classes="caption" Grid.Row="16" Grid.Column="0" Text="Dist:" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelDistanceDriven" Classes="value" Grid.Row="16" Grid.Column="1" FontSize="17" Text="-" />

        <!-- Row 17 — reset trip totals. WinForms btnTripReset @ (63,436) 76 x 44, BackgroundImage =
             Resources.back_button. Centred across both columns; click handled in code-behind. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnTripReset"
                Classes="imageButton"
                Grid.Row="17" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                Width="76"
                Height="44"
                HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Reset Trip"
                Click="btnTripReset_Click">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/back-button.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

    </Grid>

</Window>
